title: Chapter 11: Evidence, Validation, and Real-World Evaluation
---
flowchart TD
 S1["1. Formulate the evidence question\nLink intended use, comparator, population, outcome, decision consequence, and uncertainty."]
 S2["2. Map and appraise external evidence\nAssess reporting quality, risk of bias, applicability, transportability, and evidence gaps."]
 S1 --> S2
 S3["3. Plan local validation and silent-mode evaluation\nDefine cohort, data period, metrics, subgroups, workflow, human–AI interaction, and acceptance thresholds."]
 S2 --> S3
 S4["4. Select a causal evaluation design\nUse randomized, stepped-wedge, interrupted time series, difference-in-differences, target-trial, or other appropriate designs."]
 S3 --> S4
 S5["5. Collect real-world clinical and implementation evidence\nMeasure use, fidelity, adaptations, context, outcomes, workload, equity, cost, and balancing effects."]
 S4 --> S5
 S6["6. Synthesize quantitative and qualitative evidence\nIntegrate technical, clinical, economic, implementation, governance, and lived-experience findings."]
 S5 --> S6
 S7["7. Update the decision and evidence plan\nScale, modify, continue, restrict, stop, or collect additional decision-critical evidence."]
 S6 --> S7
